{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "duel-rules-3",
  "title": "duel-sim-3 issued rules snapshot",
  "description": "The immutable rules the host issues for a duel-sim-3 fight (fight-flow brief Part C, lane fight-core-1). Every number the deterministic core uses is here; none is a client constant. Units: ticks at 30 Hz, millimetres, stamina in per-mille of max, multipliers in per-mille (1150 = x1.15), HP/attack/defense in the host's absolute stat units. Rosters: 1..3 bots per side, one fielded per side at a time (bench swap with DuelSwitchRule semantics). Canonical hash: SHA-256 over ASCII 'duel-rules-3', then every rules value as int32 little-endian in FightRules.GlobalKeys order, then the fighter count (int32), then per fighter in array order: int32 id length + ASCII id + every value in FightFighterDef.Keys order. JSON key order is not significant; the hash order is. Not an authorization: the host settles only from its own replay (hard rule 1). The CPU profiles/rank rows (fight-ai-1) and duel-inputs-2 (fight-input-1) are separate contracts. Generated by Tools/FightCoreCold/gen_rules_schema.py.",
